# The Theorist, Jace Beleren's -2 has a slot for each opponent (CR 601.2c): in a three-player game Bot2's slot and Bot3's. Bot1
# chooses nothing for Bot2, whose Ornithopter is a candidate, and Bot3's Sol Ring for Bot3's slot. The target keeps its
# slot (the second, Bot3's), so it is still legal as the ability resolves: Sol Ring returns to Bot3's hand and the
# Ornithopter stays. Bot3's slot offers none of Bot2's permanents, and Bot2's none of Bot3's (the refusal).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
The Theorist, Jace Beleren
Island x4
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x6
Island x12

[Bot3 Deck]
Island
Sol Ring
Island x5
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.The Theorist, Jace Beleren.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot3.Main1]
Bot3.Hand.Island.Play
Bot3.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot3.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.The Theorist, Jace Beleren.Activate(Ability: For each opponent)
! Bot1.Target(Bot3.Battlefield.Sol Ring)
Bot1.Target()
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot3.Battlefield.Sol Ring)
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot3.Battlefield = Island
Bot3.Hand = Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Sol Ring
Bot1.Battlefield.The Theorist, Jace Beleren.Counters.Loyalty = 1
Stack.Count = 0
